{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Hypothesis confirmed, with a deterministic reproduction\n\nPosting from a parallel session that hit these same failures in an unrelated `make verify`\n(3 failed, 20648 passed, 2:18:13). This ticket is claimed elsewhere, so this is evidence\nonly — no code changed here.\n\n**The repro does not need the full suite or xdist.** Two tests, in this order, in one\nprocess, on a clean `origin/main` tree at `7c3cb5e9a4f`:\n\n```\npytest tests/interfaces/facades/test_plan_review_attestation_facades.py::test_cli_passed_but_unsigned_is_exit_11_with_byte_identical_stderr \\\n       tests/interfaces/facades/test_verify_completion_facades.py::test_cli_llm_error_is_clean_exit_one \\\n       -p no:randomly -p no:cacheprovider\n```\n\n→ `1 failed, 1 passed`. Each passes alone (16.36s and 8.92s). Reversing the pair passes.\n\n**The error is exactly the stale-stream write**, captured in full:\n\n```\n--- Logging error ---\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \".../logging/__init__.py\", line 1163, in emit\n    stream.write(msg + self.terminator)\nValueError: I/O operation on closed file.\nCall stack:\n  ...\n  File \"src/rebar/_commands/_seam.py\", line 357, in _apply_authorship\n    logger.warning(\nMessage: 'authorship: signing SKIPPED for event %s on %s — %s; writing unsigned'\n```\n\nSo the mechanism is established, not merely plausible: `_logging.py:81` binds the stream\nobject at construction, the `_HANDLER_MARKER` early-return (`:74-77`) means no later call\nrebinds it, and `logging` reports the write failure to the *current* `sys.stderr`, which the\nlater test is capturing. That stray report is what trips `\"Traceback\" not in err`.\n\nTwo notes that may save a cycle:\n\n- **Which tests fail is not stable**, because it depends on which test calls `main()` first\n  on a given xdist worker. Under `-n 4 --dist worksteal` the set varies run to run, so a\n  fix should be validated against the deterministic pair above rather than against a full\n  run coming back green once.\n- **The production path is affected too, not just tests.** Any embedder that replaces\n  `sys.stderr` after the first rebar entrypoint call keeps writing to the original stream.\n  A fix that resolves `sys.stderr` at emit time covers both; a pytest fixture that resets\n  handlers covers only the tests, and would add an `autouse_fixture` — a ratcheted mechanism\n  kind — to work around a library bug.\n\n## A third failure in the same run, probably unrelated\n\n`tests/unit/test_fetch_common_dir_coordination.py::test_uncoordinated_parallel_fetches_can_race_but_coordination_prevents_it`\nalso failed. It is undiagnosed and shares no obvious cause with this one; flagging it so a\ngreen run here is not read as covering it.\n\n## Duplicates\n\n`4c58-45d4-aaf7-48dc` (fibre-beamy-angora, open) and `7773-cca2-da72-4a0c`\n(dicey-acute-finwhale, created by this session before the match surfaced) describe the same\ndefect. Both are now linked `duplicates` to this ticket; `7773-cca2` is archived.\n"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793826038203997428,"uuid":"5171f986-b2c5-458b-b141-9b1348507f09"}